<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<c4p>
  <applications>
    <app appid="com.solaegis.dune.steam">
      <cxversion product="cxoffice">26.0</cxversion>
      <name>Dune Awakening (Steam)</name>
      <appprofile>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;Dune: Awakening via Steam in a dedicated CrossOver bottle. Uses CrossOver's built-in Steam crosstie for installation; this recipe documents post-install tuning for BattlEye and UE5 on Apple Silicon.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        <comment>20260924 - Bottle name has no colon: CrossOver strips ":" from bottle directory names. Matches task dune DUNE_BOTTLE / DUNE_DEFAULT_BOTTLE_NAME: "Dune Awakening (Steam)".</comment>
        <category>Games/Online Games</category>
        <flag>application</flag>
        <bottletemplate>win10_64</bottletemplate>
        <steamid>1172710</steamid>
      </appprofile>
      <installprofile>
        <installnotes>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bottle setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install CrossOver's built-in &lt;b&gt;Steam&lt;/b&gt; crosstie into a new bottle named &lt;b&gt;Dune Awakening (Steam)&lt;/b&gt; (no colon — CrossOver strips &lt;code&gt;:&lt;/code&gt;; matches this Crosstie and &lt;code&gt;task dune&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bottle Settings → &lt;b&gt;Graphics: D3DMetal&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Sync: MSync&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On Apple Silicon: Run with Options → Environment Variables → &lt;b&gt;Advertise AVX capabilities&lt;/b&gt; (or run &lt;code&gt;task dune:configure&lt;/code&gt; from the crossover repo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;After Steam installs Dune: Awakening&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;From the crossover repo: &lt;code&gt;task dune:fix-battleye&lt;/code&gt; — repairs BattlEye "Updating…" hangs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch via &lt;code&gt;task dune:launch:game&lt;/code&gt; (uses DuneSandbox_BE.exe).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If BattlEye still hangs: &lt;code&gt;task dune:fix-battleye --full-reset&lt;/code&gt;, then Steam → Verify integrity, re-run fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional: try a VPN during the first BattlEye update, then disconnect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Limits (read first)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Driver Load Error (1053):&lt;/b&gt; BattlEye Launcher message &lt;code&gt;Failed to initialize BattlEye Service: Driver Load Error (1053)&lt;/code&gt; means the Windows &lt;b&gt;kernel&lt;/b&gt; driver (&lt;code&gt;BEDaisy&lt;/code&gt;) failed under CrossOver/Wine. This is expected on macOS. VPN, &lt;code&gt;task dune:fix-battleye&lt;/code&gt;, and Proton BattlEye Runtime do &lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; fix it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BattlEye is kernel-level anti-cheat; CodeWeavers rates Dune: Awakening "Installs, Will Not Run". User-mode BEService repair only helps "Updating…" / installer errors, not 1053.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proton BattlEye Runtime (Steam Tools, App 1161040) is Linux-only — it does not help CrossOver on macOS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Funcom's announced single-player mode may bypass BattlEye (Conan Exiles precedent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiplayer fallback: Windows 11 ARM VM (Parallels) or cloud Windows with native BattlEye (Parallels may still hit DX12 limits).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</installnotes>
        <postdependency>com.codeweavers.c4.21821</postdependency>
      </installprofile>
    </app>
  </applications>
</c4p>
